  "_comment": "Pi 0.75.5's own catalogue stops at claude-sonnet-4-5, so the current Anthropic models are declared here (Pi otherwise passes an unknown id through with no context size or price, and the cost cap would read $0). reasoning is off on all three: Pi 0.75.5 sends thinking.type=enabled, which these models refuse with a 400 (they want thinking.type=adaptive + output_config.effort); Pi 1.4.0 may support it \u2014 then flip reasoning back on. ponytail: the prices are the 4.x generation's per million tokens until the 5.5 sheet is checked. The omlx provider is the end state (pipeline.worker-roles): not run now; the self-test loads nothing. Stage 2 (OpenRouter): prices are per million tokens from the endpoints API on 2026-10-31 for the ONE endpoint each model is pinned to by compat.openRouterRouting (sent as the request's `provider` field; allow_fallbacks false, so a down endpoint fails loudly instead of routing to another precision). contextWindow is the 64k cap the runner works to, not the model's 262k. Anthropic prices corrected 2026-10-31 to the 5.5 sheet as OpenRouter lists it for the Anthropic endpoint (Sonnet 2/10, Haiku 0.10/0.50; the 4.x rates in here before overstated Sonnet by 1.5x and Haiku by 10x, so the cost cap read high). Opus left as it was.",
